==Battleground==
*3 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 15~30 seconds<sup>450f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Gory]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Heavenly Hippoe]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Heavenly Hippoe]] spawns after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns as the boss.
**4 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**4 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Angelic Sleipnir has quite long range so bring [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]] and any other Cats that have a longer range than 372. Consider bringing [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] as a meatshield (if he is Level 30+). Also, choose Cats with [[Area Attack|Area Attacks]], good DPS, and enough range for Sleipnir, because you always want those peons killed ASAP while keeping Sleipnir from killing you.

For new players: Since this is probably the first time you've encountered Angelic Sleipnir, it is recommended to spam any [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|Anti-Angel Cats]]. Bahamut should take care of Sleipnir, so don't worry about him. Also, any [[True Form]] is recommended, especially Artist Cat's once you get it.

